Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: backpressure instead of TX drop; three QDMA reads in flight

The IQ export sends one stream at 10 GbE line rate from DRAM that the radio
is writing at 1.28 GB/s.

- With TXQ_CNGST_DROP_EN set, the QDMA silently drops frames once a TX queue
  is congested. Cleared, the ring fills and the queue stops instead, and
  every frame reaches the wire.
- MAX_ISSUE_NUM 2 limits the export to about 1.14 GB/s under that DRAM load;
  3, the field's maximum, reaches about 1.22 GB/s, line rate for 8 KiB frames.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1619,7 +1619,7 @@
 		       GLOBAL_CFG_MULTICAST_EN_MASK |
 		       GLOBAL_CFG_IRQ0_EN_MASK | GLOBAL_CFG_IRQ1_EN_MASK |
 		       GLOBAL_CFG_TX_WB_DONE_MASK |
-		       FIELD_PREP(GLOBAL_CFG_MAX_ISSUE_NUM_MASK, 2));
+		       FIELD_PREP(GLOBAL_CFG_MAX_ISSUE_NUM_MASK, 3));
 
 	airoha_qdma_init_qos(qdma);
 
@@ -1632,8 +1632,11 @@
 				  RX_DELAY_INT_MASK);
 	}
 
-	airoha_qdma_set(qdma, REG_TXQ_CNGST_CFG,
-			TXQ_CNGST_DROP_EN | TXQ_CNGST_DEI_DROP_EN);
+	/* A congested TX queue holds its descriptors, so the ring fills and the
+	 * stack sees a stopped queue, instead of the QDMA dropping silently.
+	 */
+	airoha_qdma_clear(qdma, REG_TXQ_CNGST_CFG,
+			  TXQ_CNGST_DROP_EN | TXQ_CNGST_DEI_DROP_EN);
 	airoha_qdma_init_qos_stats(qdma);
 
 	return 0;
